  "narrative": {
    "intro": "California federal contract obligations are $49.5B for FY2026 to date, with 214,210 awards and an average award size of $231K. Obligations fell 20.2% year over year. Fiscal-year trends show higher totals in prior years: FY21 was $52.1B, FY22 was $57.5B, FY23 was $61.5B, FY24 was $61.7B, and FY25 was $62B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state at $27B in obligations to date. Research and development categories lead industries, with Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $6.7B and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $5.6B. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is $4.2B and Ship Building and Repairing is $3.4B. National labs, shipbuilders, construction firms, space companies, and major universities appear among the top vendors, led by LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $3.6B and NATIONAL STEEL AND SHIPBUILDING COMPANY at $2.8B.",
