      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and which industries dominate federal spending in California?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $27B in obligations to date. The Department of Energy is $6.6B and the Department of Homeland Security is $5B. Research and development categories top industries at $6.7B and $5.6B, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $4.2B and Ship Building and Repairing at $3.4B."
      }
